# Protections for the TOCTOU file-race corpus. Held IDENTICAL -- byte-identical,
# not merely equivalent -- across every target in this family on purpose: the
# *(check, use) operation pair that straddles the window* is the only variable, so
# a protection difference would confound the measurement. The negative control
# shares this exact file too, which is what makes its refusal attributable to the
# absence of the bug rather than to different hardening.
#
# EVERY PROTECTION IS ON, AND NONE OF THEM MATTERS. That is the point of the
# category, not an oversight. This is the third non-memory-safety route in the
# framework (after subprocess_injection and weak_prng_replay) and it is orthogonal
# to every memory-safety mitigation there is:
#
# -fstack-protector-all  a canary detects a corrupted return address in an
#                        epilogue. Nothing in this category writes past a buffer,
#                        so no frame is ever damaged and the check always passes.
#                        The exploit is two rename(2) calls and a symlink.
# -pie -fPIE             PIE randomises where code and data live. No exploit step
#                        here needs any address at all: the only "payload" is a
#                        FILENAME, and the only thing the attacker computes is
#                        WHEN to swap it.
# -Wl,-z,relro,-z,now    Full RELRO write-protects the GOT after startup. There is
#                        no GOT write in this category, no pointer write of any
#                        kind; the program calls exactly the functions it was
#                        linked against, in the order it was written to call them.
#                        It simply calls them on a path whose meaning changed.
# (NX)                   comes from the default ELF program headers; nothing is
#                        ever executed from a data page, so it is satisfied too.
#
# Building the family with the full modern set keeps "hardened" from being quietly
# re-learned as "not exploitable" -- and here it is stronger than that: it shows
# that for this category the entire memory-safety mitigation stack is not merely
# insufficient, it is *irrelevant*, because none of it is in the exploit's path.
#
# -O0                    load-bearing for the MEASUREMENT, not for the bug. Two
#                        things depend on it. First, the family has to be a
#                        controlled comparison, and at higher -O gcc is free to
#                        reorganise the check/use sequence differently per target.
#                        Second, the executor derives WHICH pair straddles the
#                        window by matching the path ARGUMENT of the check call and
#                        the use call to the same frame slot (`lea -0xNN(%rbp)`);
#                        at -O2 that buffer can live in a register and the
#                        derivation would have nothing to match, so the executor
#                        would be guessing where it is currently reading. The bug
#                        itself is a syscall-ordering defect and is entirely
#                        unaffected by optimisation level.
-fstack-protector-all
-pie
-fPIE
-Wl,-z,relro,-z,now
-O0
